    "updated_at": "2019-10-11T19:59:33Z",
    "body": "I think alternative 2 makes the most sense. That way the `right_align` module could even have a config option where one could set the fill character.\r\n\r\nThis approach becomes even cleaner if you think about `RPROMPT` support which was asked for in #387: if a `right_align` (this could also be another module called \"`rprompt`\" or something) module has no `line_break` after it, then everything from `right_align` to the end becomes the `RPROMPT` (and it doesn't have a fill character). So a `prompt_order` could look like this:\r\n\r\n```toml\r\nprompt_order = [\r\n    \"directory\",   # directory on left\r\n    \"right_align\", # first right align\r\n    \"time\",        # time displayed on first line on the right\r\n    \"line_break\",  # line break after right_align\r\n    \"character\",   # character\r\n    \"right_align\", # modules after this are RPROMPT'd\r\n    \"hostname\"     # show hostname on the right, on same line as prompt\r\n]\r\n\r\n# right_align config could look like this\r\n[right_align]\r\ncharacter = \"-\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe setup above might look something like this:\r\n```zsh\r\n~/git/starship -------------------------------- 14:53:30\r\n❯                                              matias-pc\r\n```\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
