    "updated_at": "2021-04-15T11:09:16Z",
    "body": "My old bash prompt had right-aligning working with emoji and colors, so it is possible in bash too. The line that did it was\r\n`printf \"%*s\\r%s\\n\" \"$(( $(tput cols) + compensation ))\" \"${right}\" \"${left}\"` where `compensation` was the amount of non-printable chars,  `compensation=$(( ${#right} - ${#right_bw} ))` so if `right=\"^[[1mA^[[0m\"` then right_bw=\"A\" etc.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
