    "updated_at": "2021-09-07T22:41:35Z",
    "body": "Here's a workaround I have been using with some success, which is:\r\nHave a separate config file for RPROMPT (eg. `~/.config/starship-right.toml`) and just manually call Starship, eg. add to your .zshrc:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nmy_rprompt() {\r\n    STARSHIP_CONFIG=~/.config/starship-right.toml \\\r\n        starship prompt --keymap=\"$KEYMAP\" --status=\"$STARSHIP_CMD_STATUS\" --cmd-duration=\"$STARSHIP_DURATION\" --jobs=\"$STARSHIP_JOBS_COUNT\"\r\n}\r\n\r\neval \"$(starship init zsh)\"\r\nRPROMPT=\"\\$(my_rprompt)\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n(this might require that the _left_ prompt sets up any shell utility functions that the _right_ one needs, so the configs need to be somewhat compatible regarding eg. modules loaded)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
